{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/guardianship",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "guardianship"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A legal institution whereby a third party is appointed to take decisions in place of a person considered incapable of taking them on their own."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "With regard to adults with disabilities, the CRPD rejects this model of substitution of the will: art. 12 recognises their legal capacity on an equal basis and requires replacing it with support measures guided by the person's will and preferences, with safeguards against abuse, conflict of interest and undue influence. General Comment No. 1 (2014) makes clear that substitute decision-making regimes must be abolished. This sense must not be confused with the guardianship of children who lack parents exercising parental responsibility, which belongs to the field of child protection."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "10.4.1"
  ],
